@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title git post-commit — format, then lint
' purpose: why a commit still runs fmt and lint after HEAD moves, and how the hook is installed without git config
' covers: scripts/githooks/post-commit
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/hooks.go
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: internal/contract/git_hooks_test.go
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.

participant "git commit" as COMMIT <<app>>
participant ".git/hooks/post-commit" as HOOK <<app>>
participant "proveo-dev hooks post-commit" as BODY <<app>>
participant "mise run fmt" as FMT <<app>>
participant "mise run lint" as LINT <<app>>
participant "proveo-dev hooks install" as INST <<app>>

COMMIT ARROW_MAIN HOOK : HEAD already advanced
HOOK ARROW_MAIN BODY : exec mise exec -- go run
BODY ARROW_MAIN FMT
FMT ARROW_MAIN LINT : format first so lint sees it
INST ARROW_OPTIONAL HOOK : cp, chmod 0755

note right of HOOK
  **HEAD is already written.** This hook
  cannot change the commit. Format may
  dirty the tree; lint failing prints
  after the fact. SKIP_GIT_HOOKS=1
  skips both tasks.
end note

note over INST
  **No git config.** core.hooksPath is
  not set. Go copies the versioned
  shim into .git/hooks, so a clone
  still needs one command:
  mise run install-git-hooks.
end note

note right of FMT
  **Format before lint.** Lint's first
  gate is gofmt -l. Running lint first
  would fail the files fmt is about
  to rewrite. The hook does not
  git add or git commit.
end note

note right of BODY
  **A POSIX shim, a Go body.** git runs
  a hook FILE, so post-commit stays a
  6-line #!/bin/sh that execs Go; no
  host bash (host-shell-to-go P4).
end note
@enduml
